  "body": "Refs #967 (step 1 of the import: the fixture. Step 2, the import itself, is left.)\n\nClaim: mac/M1\nAuthor model: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (mac/M1-i967-sonnet)\nReviewer model: opus-5.5 (mac/M1-r1043-opus: REQUEST CHANGES on f9e5be92, APPROVE on 9f2a7d06, the head; its MANIFEST pointer detail is left for the step-2 PR)\n\n### Problem\nNo sample of the Objective-C rehost history `Documents/rehostImages.plist` existed, so the legacy import could not be tested against it.\n\n### What changed\n`tooling/legacy-oracle/samples/legacy-stores/rehost-images.archive` (binary plist), `rehost-images-empty.archive` (last image deleted), and their plutil views `rehost-images.xml.plist` and `rehost-images-empty.xml.plist`, plus a MANIFEST row and note. Made by the unmodified `Classes/RehostImage.m` @ `87fe0d1c`, archived with the same call as `RehostImageViewController.m:165-166` (`archivedDataWithRootObject:` on an `NSMutableArray`). Three images with fake ids (`aaaaaaaa`...), fake dates, covering (images 2 and 3 hold synthetic states no legacy writer produces, marked as such in the MANIFEST): numeric width/height, an archived `NSNull` for medium (what the real host answer yields), nil preview, nil width/height, `deleted`, `version` 2. The throwaway harness (stubs for the UIKit-free dependencies it links but never calls) is not committed; its command line is in the MANIFEST note. No network, no account, no secret.\n\n### Tests\nDocs and data only. `plutil -p` / `-lint` checked, class names and keys compared with `encodeWithCoder:`, grep for non-fake values. `pre-commit run --all-files` green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n\n",
