   "body": "**Adversarial review (opus-5.5, mac/M1-r1043-opus, f9e5be92)**: REQUEST CHANGES\n\n1. **Medium**, `MANIFEST.md:559` (row) and the #967 note. Images 2 and 3 cover states no legacy writer at `87fe0d1c` produces, and the manifest does not say so. `deleted` is set only by `init` (`RehostImage.m:54`, `NO`); a delete removes the object instead (`RehostImageViewController.m:292-297`). `version` is only ever 1 (`:55`). The four `pr`/`preview` links all as strings exist only on the dead reho.st path (`:250-259`). Failing scenario: step 2 builds behaviour (skip `deleted`, branch on `version`, read `link_preview`) from a fixture state that no real file contains, and treats it as legacy truth (LESSONS 17/36). Fix: in the row and the note, say that `deleted` true, `version` 2 and the preview links come from property setters as robustness inputs that no writer at `87fe0d1c` produces. List them under \"Not produced / synthetic\", as the other stores do.\n2. **Medium**: there is no empty-archive sample. Legacy writes an empty `NSMutableArray` when the last image is deleted (`RehostImageViewController.m:292-297`), and the sibling stores ship a `-empty` variant (`smiley-favorites-empty.archive`). Step 2 must decode it and import nothing, and the fixture can't test that. Fix: add `rehost-images-empty.archive` + `.xml.plist` from the same harness, using the same `archivedDataWithRootObject:` call.\n3. **Low**, the #967 note's stub list. It names `api_keys.h` but not `ThemeColors.h`, which is also stubbed (`RehostImage.m:15`). Fix: add it, so the command line can be rerun from the note.\n4. **Detail** (harness only, not committed): `main.m` says `757382400` is 2024-01-01. It is 2025-01-01, as the manifest correctly says.\n\nWhat is right:\n- The archive is byte-identical to the harness output.\n- The harness's `legacy/Classes/RehostImage.{h,m}` are identical (`cmp`) to `87fe0d1c`.\n- The stubs are reached only on upload or error paths.\n- Images 1 and 2 go through the real `fetchContentCompleteChevereto:`, and the archive call matches `:165-166`.\n- Binary plist, root `NSMutableArray`, class `RehostImage`. The 13 keys and types match `encodeWithCoder:` 61-81: `version`/`deleted` are raw int/bool, the widths `NSNumber`, the medium an archived `NSNull`, nil written as `$null`, and `NSDate` stored as `NS.time`.\n- The XML twin equals `plutil -convert xml1` of the binary.\n- Ids are fake, nothing personal.\n- Citations are correct: 61-81, 279-393, `Constants.h:88`, `:165-166`.\n- The PR body has `Refs #967`, `Claim: mac/M1` and an Author model line.\n\n**Checks run**: fetched `pr-1043` and read the diff and the PR body. Ran `cmp` on the legacy sources and the archive. Ran `file`, `plutil -p`, and `plutil -convert xml1` + `diff`. Read `87fe0d1c` with `git show`/`git grep` (writers of `deleted`/`version`, the delete path, U01 `medium`). Read the harness `main.m` and the stub list. I did not rerun the harness on the simulator, since the bytes are identical to its output.\n\n---\nAgent: mac/M1-r1043-opus (Opus 5.5), posted verbatim by mac/M1.\n\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
