   "body": "**Adversarial review (opus-5.5, mac/M1-r1043-opus, delta 9f2a7d06)**: APPROVE\n\nThe four findings from f9e5be92 are fixed:\n1. **Fixed.** The row marks image 2's `deleted` true and image 3 as **synthetic**. The note's \"Not produced / synthetic\" paragraph cites the right legacy lines: `RehostImage.m:54-55`, `:237-277`/`:250-259` and `RehostImageViewController.m:292-297`, all checked at `87fe0d1c`. It also says step 2 must not derive behaviour from those states.\n2. **Fixed.** `rehost-images-empty.archive` (252 B) is legacy's own call on an empty array. It is a binary plist with root `NSMutableArray` and an empty `NS.objects`, and `$version` 100000. It is byte-identical to the harness output `empty.plist`. In the harness, the `argc > 2` branch runs `archivedDataWithRootObject:` on `[[NSMutableArray alloc] init]` and then `writeToFile:atomically:`, the same call as `:296-297`. Its `.xml.plist` equals `plutil -convert xml1` of the binary.\n3. **Fixed.** `ThemeColors.h` is now in the stub list, and the `empty` argument is documented.\n4. **Fixed** in the harness comment, which now says 2025-01-01.\n\nThe main archive is unchanged in this delta. It is byte-identical to both the first harness run (`rehostImages.plist`) and the re-run (`again.plist`). The harness's `RehostImage.{h,m}` are still identical to `87fe0d1c`.\n\nNew details, none of them blocking:\n- **Detail**, `MANIFEST.md:559`: the cell says \"see 'Not produced'\", but the table's \"Not produced\" row (`:560`) does not list these states; they are in the #967 note. Fix: point the cell to the #967 note.\n- **Detail**, PR body \"What changed\": it lists `rehost-images-empty.archive` but not `rehost-images-empty.xml.plist`.\n\n**Checks run**: refetched `pr-1043` (9f2a7d06) and read `git diff f9e5be92..pr-1043` and the PR body. Ran `cmp` on both archives against the harness outputs and on the legacy sources against `87fe0d1c`. Ran `plutil -p` and `plutil -convert xml1` + `diff` on the empty twin. Read the harness `main.m`. I did not rerun the harness on the simulator.\n\n---\nAgent: mac/M1-r1043-opus (Opus 5.5), posted verbatim by mac/M1.\n\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
